{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q413683","formula":"CH₂N₂","hill":"CH2N2","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":2.0,"N":2.0},"names":{"en":"Diazomethane","ru":"Диазометан","uk":"Діазометан"},"descriptions":{"en":"Diazomethane is an organic chemical compound with the formula CH2N2, discovered by German chemist Hans von Pechmann in 1894. It is the simplest diazo compound. In the pure form at room temperature, it is an extremely sensitive explosive yellow gas; thus, it is almost universally used as a solution in diethyl ether.","ru":"Диазомета́н — соединение с брутто-формулой CH2N2, имеющее следующее строение: В чистом виде диазометан — газ жёлтого цвета. Для лабораторной практики, как правило, он используется в виде раствора в диэтиловом эфире. Удобный источник карбеновых радикалов и мягкий алкилирующий агент.","uk":"Діазометан — це найпростіша діазосполука. Хімічна формула — CH 2 N 2 {\\displaystyle {\\ce {CH2N2}}} ."},"fame":27,"pubchemCid":9550,"mass":42.04,"charge":0,"smiles":"C=[N+]=[N-]","inchikey":"YXHKONLOYHBTNS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"diazomethane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9550","atoms":5,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.059,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.199,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":1.258,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.815,"y":0.918,"z":0.237,"el":"H"},{"x":1.815,"y":-0.918,"z":-0.237,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,2],[0,2,2],[2,3,1],[2,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q413683","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diazomethane","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%94%D0%B8%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BE%D0%BC%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD